1
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:06,970
JoJo...

2
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:10,600
I've heard so much about you.

3
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:15,520
Listen, and listen good.

4
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:21,260
San Viento here, the so-called Pillar Man,
uses a mask to turn men into vampires.

5
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:25,168
He does this to make them
stronger, and then he devours them.

6
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:26,260
Destroy him!

7
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:28,675
Take him out while there's still time!

8
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:33,939
Don't do it, Jojo!

9
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:34,942
He's dangerous!

10
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:40,590
You're it!

11
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:44,980
Oh, I get it.

12
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:47,597
You're one of those strong
silent types, right?

13
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,037
Ever thought about modeling?

14
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:50,657
You've got a nice look there.

15
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:52,177
Come on, let's see what you've got.

16
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:53,201
Give me a smile.

17
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:54,980
I know you can do it.

18
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:56,708
Show me some vulnerability.

19
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:57,757
Work with me here.

20
00:00:57,840 --> 00:01:01,920
Make some love to the camera.
Ready? Sit! Give me happy!

21
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:02,980
Now be silly!

22
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,960
Show us those pearly whites!

23
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:39,120
Come on, big guy.

24
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:41,300
Smile at the birdie. Jojo!

25
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:43,177
Stop this nonsense immediately!

26
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:44,177
Don't provoke him!

27
00:02:44,260 --> 00:02:47,080
Please, Jojo, send me
into his dangerous! Yeah.

28
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:51,657
I know you think he's dangerous, but I
have a theory that maybe he's not so bad.

29
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:53,317
Let me test something out here.

30
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:57,177
I don't want to assume he's evil just
because he killed a bunch of brainless...

31
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:58,495
What are you, insane?

32
00:02:58,740 --> 00:03:02,320
If he's not evil, why did he
kill all my men? Don't know.

33
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:05,157
Some would say you're
responsible for what's happened.

34
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:07,097
Weren't you the one
experimenting on him and

35
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:09,397
trying to blast him
away in the first place?

36
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:11,417
Not that I really care about that.

37
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:13,497
The only reason I'm here
is to make sure that

38
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:16,639
Speedwagon makes it back
to New York safe and south.

39
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:18,720
Anyway, I'm not here to fight.

40
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:20,500
And I'm feeling generous.

41
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:22,700
Come on, loosen up, big guy.

42
00:03:22,940 --> 00:03:24,480
How about that smile?

43
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:31,697
That was rude.

44
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:34,357
He just walked through me
like I wasn't even there.

45
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:36,637
Who the hell does this guy think he is?

46
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:38,897
Maybe I should teach him a quick lesson.

47
00:03:38,980 --> 00:03:40,297
Have a nice trip.

48
00:03:40,380 --> 00:03:46,697
What the

49
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:47,610
hell was that?

50
00:03:47,693 --> 00:03:50,860
That was the weirdest feeling and it hurt.

51
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:00,080
What is this?

52
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:05,160
This tool, cold and long,
with many different pieces.

53
00:04:05,380 --> 00:04:06,498
He does understand!

54
00:04:06,620 --> 00:04:08,160
He's not simply mimicking!

55
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:12,734
It took him practically no time at
all to completely master our language!

56
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:17,070
How...

57
00:04:17,153 --> 00:04:18,400
how is he doing that?

58
00:04:19,220 --> 00:04:20,220
He took it apart.

59
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:23,577
He dismantled that entire weapon
like some expert gunsmith.

60
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:28,357
It takes a soldier dozens of hours to learn
how to fieldstrip his weapon that fast.

61
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:31,616
He's using his advanced
intellect to learn everything.

62
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:33,840
So bright.

63
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:36,540
This light is new to me.

64
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:38,960
What is it? Don't you see?

65
00:04:39,100 --> 00:04:41,688
We weren't the ones
observing all this time.

66
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:44,200
He was actually watching us.

67
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:46,760
Hey, big guy.

68
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:48,537
You want to learn a new joke?

69
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:51,057
Just stop me if you've
heard this one before.

70
00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:51,970
Knock, knock.

71
00:04:52,053 --> 00:04:52,883
Knock, knock.

72
00:04:53,660 --> 00:04:54,680
Jojo, get away!

73
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:58,501
You are playing games, Primitive.

74
00:04:58,620 --> 00:05:01,280
I do not want to play games.

75
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:05,380
What the?

76
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:10,480
Ribblades, sometimes
known as fighting ribs.

77
00:05:11,260 --> 00:05:14,820
They're capable of being
manipulated in any direction. Jojo!

78
00:05:25,020 --> 00:05:26,460
Sparks energy.

79
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:30,420
This human seems
different from the others.

80
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:34,540
I was not able to absorb
his body into mine.

81
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:36,680
He just flew away.

82
00:05:37,860 --> 00:05:41,120
And somehow, his leg, it remains.

83
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:42,760
It still seems fine.

84
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:45,540
This one is something new.

85
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:48,360
I have yet to see such a human.

86
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,437
Is he a unique specimen?

87
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:55,580
Or do all humans of his particular
class possess the same properties?

88
00:05:56,020 --> 00:05:58,040
Could it be related to age?

89
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:05,420
Ah, now I see.

90
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:07,260
My instinct was right.

91
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,540
That human is unique.

92
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:12,260
Jojo, please!

93
00:06:12,620 --> 00:06:14,200
Make it stop, please!

94
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:18,637
Speed wagon!

95
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:20,680
That bastard!

96
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:23,440
Let the old man go, San Viento!

97
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:25,780
Now I'm in the mood!

98
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:29,025
Come on, big guy, you
wanna try and take me on?

99
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:34,640
It would seem that humans
have evolved their confidence.

100
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:38,060
Hope you're hungry!

101
00:06:38,860 --> 00:06:41,400
One Hamon sandwich coming up!

102
00:06:45,620 --> 00:06:46,450
Huh?

103
00:06:46,533 --> 00:06:47,363
What the devil?

104
00:06:47,446 --> 00:06:49,540
My Harmon is making that blood float.

105
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:54,153
Something's wrong here.

106
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:57,940
My Harmon is running off him
like rain off a raincoat.

107
00:06:58,340 --> 00:07:01,777
He's somehow repelling it and
pushing it into all of this blood.

108
00:07:01,860 --> 00:07:03,240
I don't understand it.

109
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:05,580
His skin is acting like a ground.

110
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,824
Somehow it's behaving
just like Straitzo's scar.

111
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:13,940
My body and his body seem to be
repelling against one another.

112
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:20,230
Whoa!

113
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:21,510
What?

114
00:07:21,593 --> 00:07:23,025
What have you done to my hand?

115
00:07:24,140 --> 00:07:24,970
Wait.

116
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:29,860
It's still there.

117
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,080
But check it out.

118
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:34,957
I can completely remove my thumb.

119
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:37,037
Doesn't anyone have a sense of humor left?

120
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:37,950
Come on, guys.

121
00:07:38,033 --> 00:07:39,291
This is funny stuff here.

122
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:43,200
But seriously, folks.

123
00:07:43,460 --> 00:07:45,497
Lucky thing I rolled
my wrist just in time.

124
00:07:45,580 --> 00:07:47,500
The beast's immune to Hamon.

125
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:49,440
That's not true, Jojo!

126
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:51,200
Don't you see?

127
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:53,417
It was Hamon that was protecting you!

128
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:57,324
It kept your body from being
completely absorbed into that thing!

129
00:07:57,420 --> 00:07:58,250
Idiot!

130
00:07:58,333 --> 00:08:00,218
It's like eating a blowfish for him!

131
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:04,120
He knows he must kill it first
and then remove the poison part!

132
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:07,800
That is how San Viento plans
on absorbing Jojo's body!

133
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:13,197
Well, too bad for him I'm not a blowfish.

134
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:16,057
Regardless, I need to think
of something fast here.

135
00:08:16,140 --> 00:08:18,537
Maybe it's time to make
my emergency escape.

136
00:08:18,620 --> 00:08:19,679
You can't do that!

137
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:22,577
The danger of San Viento
escaping is too high!

138
00:08:22,660 --> 00:08:24,425
No one leaves until he's dead!

139
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:25,370
Oh, shut up!

140
00:08:25,453 --> 00:08:26,283
You released this monster,

141
00:08:26,366 --> 00:08:29,177
and now you're saying you need
someone else to clean up the mess?

142
00:08:29,260 --> 00:08:32,378
I don't need anything else
on my plate, Von Stroheim!

143
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:41,051
Let's see if I can inject some hormone
into his system with something sharp!

144
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:46,560
His skin is malleable like rubber.

145
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:49,620
See if you can dodge this one, big guy!

146
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:52,237
How about a dose of
hormone right in the eye?

147
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:55,202
I hope you're ready for
your can't-miss close-up!

148
00:08:57,940 --> 00:08:58,770
What?

149
00:08:58,853 --> 00:08:59,683
That's impossible!

150
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:02,337
Even his eyes feel like
they're some kind of rubber!

151
00:09:02,420 --> 00:09:04,361
Jojo, get out of there right now!

152
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:08,870
Jojo!

153
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:13,200
That hit to the solar plexus
completely knocked the wind out of him!

154
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:18,460
He seems to create his own energy.

155
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:20,900
He controls it with his breathing.

156
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:27,120
But lying there now, unconscious, he
is as vulnerable as any other human.

157
00:09:27,920 --> 00:09:28,750
Jojo!

158
00:09:28,833 --> 00:09:31,232
You've got to use your harm on breathing!

159
00:09:34,780 --> 00:09:36,074
You've got to breathe!

160
00:09:37,780 --> 00:09:39,368
Use your harm on breathing!

161
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:40,640
Breathe, damn it!

162
00:09:40,740 --> 00:09:41,570
Breathe!

163
00:09:41,653 --> 00:09:42,483
No!

164
00:09:42,566 --> 00:09:43,780
There's no stopping him!

165
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:46,666
I've got to initiate a
self-destruct sequence!

166
00:09:53,040 --> 00:09:54,580
For the Fatherland!

167
00:09:56,940 --> 00:09:58,920
I wouldn't do that if I were you!

168
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:02,186
Everyone just calm down here.

169
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:04,340
Looks like my gamble paid off.

170
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:07,097
Figuring that attacks
from outside are no good,

171
00:10:07,180 --> 00:10:10,497
I'm going to send some Hamon into
him while he tries to enjoy his meal!

172
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:11,410
Jojo!

173
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:14,874
I waited for you to start devouring me.

174
00:10:15,040 --> 00:10:16,275
This is gonna be fun!

175
00:10:16,700 --> 00:10:18,600
Enjoy your Hamon Blast!

176
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:37,570
I...

177
00:10:37,653 --> 00:10:38,483
I think I get it.

178
00:10:38,566 --> 00:10:41,317
Now that I've seen him from
the inside, I understand.

179
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:44,120
His whole body is one
big digestive system.

180
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:48,177
Every one of his cells, they're all
filled with aggressive digestive enzymes,

181
00:10:48,260 --> 00:10:50,477
making it possible to dissolve his prey.

182
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:54,972
It looks like he's absorbing them, when
actually he's digesting them whole.

183
00:10:55,860 --> 00:10:59,000
Harmon, that was what kept
me from being digested.

184
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:01,717
I sent it inside him
when he tried to eat me.

185
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,920
Jojo, your Harmon wasn't enough.

186
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:07,434
You have to find a way to
completely destroy San Viento.

187
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:23,997
The separated parts of San Viento
are trying to connect to one another.

188
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:26,637
That's pretty much exactly
what happened with Streetser.

189
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:30,077
Lucky me, I figured you would
try to go and do the same thing.

190
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:31,220
Von Stroheim!

191
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:38,622
Come on, get a hold of yourself!

192
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:40,858
Does this thing have any weaknesses?

193
00:11:41,140 --> 00:11:43,300
Uh, sunlight, yeah! That's it!

194
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:45,880
It was there, on the walls of the cave.

195
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:47,980
Sunlight is his natural enemy.

196
00:11:48,340 --> 00:11:52,811
The very reason he made the masks in
the first place was to conquer the sun!

197
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:01,140
Are you insane?

198
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:02,418
What are you doing?

199
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:06,037
You can't let San Viento
escape into the outside world!

200
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:10,020
On the contrary, I think he needs
to go on a nice sunlit stroll.

201
00:12:14,660 --> 00:12:16,248
He's running out of breath.

202
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:19,273
He won't be able to control his harmone.

203
00:12:19,420 --> 00:12:21,237
He hasn't had enough training with it.

204
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,673
This fight has completely exhausted him.

205
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:28,300
Cease this foolishness
now, you lowly primitive.

206
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:37,830
Remember!

207
00:12:37,913 --> 00:12:39,817
You must control your hormone breathing!

208
00:12:39,900 --> 00:12:43,517
If I could breathe, I probably wouldn't
be so tired in the first place!

209
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:44,640
Come on, big guy!

210
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:47,800
I think we've all had
just about enough of you!

211
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:49,677
But fortunately for me,

212
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:53,936
we're just a few steps away from the
two of us catching some nice rays!

213
00:12:59,660 --> 00:13:00,820
What the hell?

214
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:04,500
I can't move!

215
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:05,720
I feel so heavy!

216
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:07,590
What?

217
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:09,120
What's happening to me?

218
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:13,420
Meat invade, also known as foul flesh.

219
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:16,100
They're pieces of his flesh!

220
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:18,230
They're...

221
00:13:18,313 --> 00:13:19,620
they're feeding on me!

222
00:13:21,220 --> 00:13:22,050
You...

223
00:13:22,133 --> 00:13:23,320
you son of a...

224
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:26,180
Got to stay focused!

225
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:32,100
I never once imagined a human such as
you would be born during my slumber.

226
00:13:38,140 --> 00:13:38,970
What?

227
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:53,580
Joestar, leave the rest to me,
Colonel Rudolf von Stroheim.

228
00:13:54,260 --> 00:13:56,319
Opening the door will end all this.

229
00:13:56,560 --> 00:13:59,440
Allow me to help you
destroy this vile creature.

230
00:14:00,020 --> 00:14:01,320
Wow, von Stroheim.

231
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:03,148
I would have never thought.

232
00:14:03,580 --> 00:14:06,860
Hm, well-attempted, primitives.

233
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:19,300
I can almost reach the door!

234
00:14:20,920 --> 00:14:22,860
A meaningless struggle.

235
00:14:28,380 --> 00:14:30,320
This is bad.

236
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:32,560
Joestar, get up!

237
00:14:32,860 --> 00:14:34,637
Don't just lie there like a baby.

238
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:36,191
I'm trying to think here.

239
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:38,697
If you hadn't noticed,
we're both in deep trouble.

240
00:14:38,780 --> 00:14:39,610
Silence!

241
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:42,666
Do you see those axes
on the wall next to you?

242
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:44,220
Reach up and grab one.

243
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:46,540
Take one and chop off my leg.

244
00:14:46,740 --> 00:14:48,180
I can't do that.

245
00:14:48,380 --> 00:14:50,137
You coward, cut off my leg.

246
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:52,897
It's the only way we're
getting that door open.

247
00:14:52,980 --> 00:14:55,880
Maybe you're right, but
are you sure about this?

248
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,057
I mean, there has got
to be some other way.

249
00:14:58,140 --> 00:14:59,360
Do as I say.

250
00:14:59,660 --> 00:15:01,317
He's recovering, Joestar.

251
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:03,040
But I'm no doctor!

252
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:05,217
I have no idea how to do this right!

253
00:15:05,300 --> 00:15:08,080
I am a proud servant of the Wehrmacht!

254
00:15:08,260 --> 00:15:11,789
I am prepared to do whatever
is required to fulfill my duty!

255
00:15:12,220 --> 00:15:14,737
I proudly give up my
leg for the Fatherland!

256
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:16,820
Now hurry up before it's too late!

257
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:18,410
Damn it!

258
00:15:18,493 --> 00:15:19,820
Do it now, Joestar!

259
00:15:22,300 --> 00:15:23,580
Okay, I'll do it!

260
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,240
If you really want me to chop
it off, then off it goes!

261
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:29,217
I demand that you chop it off now!

262
00:15:29,300 --> 00:15:30,130
Ow!

263
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:34,977
I figured this guy was just some bloated
power monger, but I gotta hand it to him.

264
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:36,180
He's got guts.

265
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:42,060
I wish there was some other way, but if
he's courageous enough, then forgive me!

266
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:00,690
Aaaaah!

267
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:08,512
Tell me big guy, how does that
sunshine feel on your skin?

268
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:10,070
Aaaaah!

269
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:13,220
He did it!

270
00:16:21,060 --> 00:16:22,200
What's he doing?

271
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:26,190
Aaaaaah!

272
00:16:26,273 --> 00:16:27,340
Help me!

273
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:30,117
That monster's trying
to crawl inside my leg!

274
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:31,494
Get out of there, you!

275
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,680
Whoa, this is a shock.

276
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:39,553
Von Stroheim's basically okay,
and he's free of any harm.

277
00:16:45,140 --> 00:16:45,970
Damn it!

278
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:48,200
You get out of me! Run, Viento!

279
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:51,500
I can't believe this thing's willpower.

280
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:53,701
I've never seen anything like it.

281
00:16:56,060 --> 00:17:00,797
If he stays inside von Stroheim, he'll be
totally fine even here in broad daylight!

282
00:17:00,880 --> 00:17:02,360
I can feel him!

283
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:03,980
This can't be real!

284
00:17:04,420 --> 00:17:07,497
Do you want to know what the
worst part about this is?

285
00:17:07,580 --> 00:17:09,800
My leg doesn't even hurt anymore!

286
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:12,680
It feels pleasant, you believe that?

287
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:14,060
Oh my god!

288
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,280
Von Stroheim!

289
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:31,800
Wait, what are you doing?

290
00:17:32,400 --> 00:17:34,900
Put it down, Von Stroheim! Stay back!

291
00:17:36,620 --> 00:17:40,360
You've seen what horrible
things San Viento is capable of!

292
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:41,980
There is no hope!

293
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:44,004
My destiny has been determined!

294
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:48,160
So now, all I can do is
destroy the both of us!

295
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:53,417
But I have one more thing to say
to you before my time is done!

296
00:17:53,500 --> 00:17:57,324
If you know what's good for you,
you'll listen close, Englishman.

297
00:17:58,860 --> 00:18:04,300
We did not awaken San Viento simply for
scientific research or military gain.

298
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:06,260
Then why?

299
00:18:06,480 --> 00:18:08,400
Why did you risk it? Tell me!

300
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:09,810
Silence!

301
00:18:09,893 --> 00:18:13,487
It's your destiny to hear these
words from my lips, Joe Starr.

302
00:18:13,740 --> 00:18:16,197
San Viento is just the tip of the iceberg.

303
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:18,797
The Wehrmacht has discovered
another pillar in Europe.

304
00:18:18,880 --> 00:18:22,821
We now know that San Viento is not
the only one of his kind around.

305
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:28,377
Wait so there's more of them
where are they tell me Von

306
00:18:28,460 --> 00:18:31,897
Stroheim where I'm sorry but I
don't have that answer for you

307
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:35,057
Joestar there are more pillar
men out there and they have

308
00:18:35,140 --> 00:18:38,637
powers that are beyond our
wildest imagination for millennia

309
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:41,657
those powers have remained
dormant but that won't last and

310
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:44,797
soon they will awaken you must
find another weakness other

311
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:49,437
than just sunlight or else
hope is lost that's why we were

312
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:52,957
experimenting on San Viento we
were looking for that weakness.

313
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:56,097
There's a battle against the
Pillar Man yet to be fought.

314
00:18:56,180 --> 00:18:59,517
The events of 50 years ago
call upon you for that battle.

315
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:00,660
Listen to me.

316
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:04,313
You will need more than just
your Hamon to overcome them.

317
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:06,440
You must go to Rome.

318
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:09,257
There you will find
someone who can help you.

319
00:19:09,340 --> 00:19:12,880
It is someone that your
speed wagon knows very well.

320
00:19:15,300 --> 00:19:20,897
San Viento is trying to move my party
into that well so he can hide again.

321
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:26,820
But he can't stop me from opening up my
body completely to let the sun shine in!

322
00:19:30,940 --> 00:19:33,800
Von Stroheim, don't you dare.

323
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:41,460
Human greatness lies in having the
courage to face down one's fears.

324
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:43,369
Do you know who said that?

325
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:45,266
The Greek historian Plutarch.

326
00:19:49,120 --> 00:19:49,950
Farewell.

327
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:52,660
You annoying Englishman!

328
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:53,980
Don't do it!

329
00:19:54,080 --> 00:19:55,637
I still have questions for you!

330
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:56,550
Monster!

331
00:20:00,160 --> 00:20:02,920
Damn that crazy German and all his honor!

332
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:07,586
I'm sure that we could
have found another way!

333
00:20:21,360 --> 00:20:22,260
Cezriato!

334
00:20:24,860 --> 00:20:25,720
You annoy me!

335
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:28,960
Primitive, I will destroy you!

336
00:20:29,340 --> 00:20:30,634
Steady your breathing.

337
00:20:30,820 --> 00:20:32,408
Use your hormone technique.

338
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:49,537
Primitive, why oppose me?

339
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:51,800
You were doomed here from the start!

340
00:20:52,460 --> 00:20:53,290
Ha!

341
00:20:53,373 --> 00:20:55,537
I know just what you're going to say next!

342
00:20:55,620 --> 00:20:58,777
You'll say I've seen right through
you all this time, Joestar!

343
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:01,860
I've seen right through
you all this time, Joestar!

344
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:09,480
It's high noon over this well!

345
00:21:09,740 --> 00:21:12,917
The sun reflecting off of the
water should cook you nicely!

346
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,457
Although I doubt you even thought of that!

347
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:17,537
You were thinking about jumping under the

348
00:21:17,620 --> 00:21:20,017
night's cool water and
getting out of the sun,

349
00:21:20,100 --> 00:21:20,930
right?

350
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:24,400
Well, screw that idea!

351
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:26,940
I'm not letting you touch the water!

352
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:47,477
I'm alive, thanks to the sun.

353
00:21:47,560 --> 00:21:49,457
He's a statue now.

354
00:21:49,540 --> 00:21:50,377
But!

355
00:21:50,460 --> 00:21:53,180
We finally got that smile.

356
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:14,177
I'll be the roundabout.

357
00:22:14,260 --> 00:22:17,137
The words will make you.

358
00:22:17,220 --> 00:22:18,337
Out and out!

359
00:22:18,420 --> 00:22:21,640
I spend the day your way.

360
00:22:23,580 --> 00:22:25,037
Call it morning.

361
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:26,437
Driving through the sun.

362
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:28,120
And in and out the valley.

363
00:22:37,620 --> 00:22:41,177
The music dance and sing.

364
00:22:41,260 --> 00:22:45,377
They make the children really ring.

365
00:22:45,460 --> 00:22:49,520
I'll spend the day your way.

366
00:22:50,840 --> 00:22:53,537
Cold and mooding, driving through the sun.

367
00:22:53,620 --> 00:22:55,520
And in and out the valley.

368
00:22:57,400 --> 00:23:00,000
In and out around the lake.

369
00:23:01,180 --> 00:23:03,397
Mountains come out of the sky.

370
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:05,080
And they'll stand there.

371
00:23:08,240 --> 00:23:10,377
When my lover will be there.

372
00:23:10,460 --> 00:23:11,840
And we'll see you?

373
00:23:30,140 --> 00:23:32,200
My grandfather died tragically.

374
00:23:32,340 --> 00:23:34,417
You couldn't even beat
one of those pigeons.

375
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:36,760
Quickly, bring out more UV lamps.

376
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:38,020
Now is the time.

377
00:23:38,380 --> 00:23:39,640
Awaken, my masters.

378
00:23:41,840 --> 00:23:42,670
Amen.
